It's been so much fun to go episode by episode with you through my favorite show of all time.
和你一起一集一集地观看我最喜欢的节目真是太有趣了。

00:47:18.500 --> 00:47:21.539
In fall 2005, I was a freshman in high school.
2005年秋天，我还是一名高中新生。

00:47:21.539 --> 00:47:27.500
I convinced my parents that we should watch the pilot during dinner and my John dropped with the Aunt Robin reveal.
我说服了我的父母，我们应该在晚餐时观看试播集，而我的约翰则随罗宾阿姨的揭晓而落下。

00:47:27.500 --> 00:47:28.619
That's in the pilot, right?
那是在飞行员中，对吧？

00:47:28.619 --> 00:47:34.659
The very end of the pilot, armed with a VCR, later a TiVo that could burn DVDs ooh fancy.
飞行员的最后配备了录像机，后来又配备了可以刻录 DVD 的 TiVo，太棒了。

00:47:34.659 --> 00:47:37.420
I made sure that my friend group didn't miss an episode.
我确保我的朋友群没有错过任何一集。

00:47:37.420 --> 00:47:40.820
By the time the show was syndicated on lifetime, we were sitting in many places.
当这部剧在《一生》上播出时，我们已经坐在很多地方了。

00:47:40.820 --> 00:47:42.940
One of them was lifetime, weirdly.
奇怪的是，其中之一是一生。

00:47:42.940 --> 00:47:46.099
I had already memorized several of my favorite episodes.
我已经记住了我最喜欢的几集。

00:47:46.099 --> 00:47:49.099
Hemium became the shorthand to talk about our lives.
Hemium 成为谈论我们生活的代名词。

00:47:49.099 --> 00:47:52.380
If someone was a little too obsessed with fairness, they were a lily.
如果有人过于执着于公平，那么他就是一朵百合花。

00:47:52.380 --> 00:47:55.980
When I had a crush on someone new, they would try to rein in my tit.
当我暗恋一个新人时，他们会试图控制我的乳头。

00:47:55.980 --> 00:47:58.900
We burned copies of the get psyched mix and had them in our first cars.
我们刻录了令人兴奋的混音副本，并将它们放在我们的第一辆汽车中。

00:47:58.900 --> 00:48:09.346
I got a 98% on an essay, my sophomore year of college, how Hymnium was a classic buildings Roman using post-modern storytelling happy to share the final draft please do by the way please send that to us.
我在大学二年级的一篇论文上获得了 98% 的成绩，《Hymnium》是如何使用后现代故事讲述的罗马经典建筑，很高兴分享最终稿，请顺便将其发送给我们。

00:48:09.346 --> 00:48:16.860
The finale aired during the first year of what would eventually be a seven year journey to get my masters and my PhD in speech language pathology.
结局在我最终获得言语病理学硕士和博士学位的七年旅程的第一年播出。

00:48:17.500 --> 00:48:20.961
I entered the age where the characters start when I needed the most.
我在最需要的时候进入了人物开始的年龄。

00:48:20.961 --> 00:48:26.460
I had my first major depressive episode I gained weight I dealt with loss and separation for the first time.
我第一次经历了严重的抑郁症，我体重增加了，我第一次面对失去和分离。

00:48:27.099 --> 00:48:35.599
Hymnium showed me that all of these things could happen and helped me to handle them with with as much grace as I could, though along the way I felt myself becoming jaded.
Hymnium 向我展示了所有这些事情都可能发生，并帮助我尽可能优雅地处理它们，尽管一路上我感觉自己变得厌倦了。

00:48:35.599 --> 00:48:43.980
In 2020, as I finished my dissertation, I purposely decided to control what I could and live my life out of order.
2020年，当我完成论文时，我故意决定控制我能控制的事情，过着没有秩序的生活。

00:48:43.980 --> 00:48:47.820
I was ready to be a dad and so I signed up to be a foster parent.
我已经准备好成为一名父亲，所以我报名成为一名养父母。

00:48:47.820 --> 00:48:54.380
I finished my dissertation and the foster care classes during lockdown and accepted my first case the day after I defended.
我在封锁期间完成了论文和寄养课程，并在辩护后的第二天接受了我的第一个案件。

00:48:54.380 --> 00:49:02.820
Though I experienced more trials with navigating the beginning of my career in foster children, My wonderful son, Jackson, came into my life in June, 2022.
尽管我在寄养儿童职业生涯的初期经历了更多的考验，但我的好儿子杰克逊于 2022 年 6 月进入了我的生活。

00:49:02.820 --> 00:49:06.139
His adoption will be finalized around October.
他的收养将于十月左右完成。

00:49:06.139 --> 00:49:11.920
In a very Ted-like roundabout way, that does lead me to my recent reembrace of my inner Ted at 34.
以一种非常像 Ted 的迂回方式，这确实让我最近重新拥抱了 34 岁时内心的 Ted。

00:49:11.920 --> 00:49:16.119
When I met my new coworker, Kat, in 2021, she was engaged.
2021 年，当我遇到新同事 Kat 时，她已经订婚了。

00:49:16.119 --> 00:49:19.599
Eight months after her wedding, Kat Mose beat me.
结婚八个月后，凯特·摩西殴打了我。

00:49:19.599 --> 00:49:21.360
She told me that she loved me.
她告诉我她爱我。

00:49:21.360 --> 00:49:25.440
I told her that we had to stop hanging out because it violated the terms of her relationship.
我告诉她我们必须停止出去玩，因为这违反了她的关系条款。

00:49:25.440 --> 00:49:27.480
She told me that she and her husband were separating.
她告诉我她和她丈夫正在分居。

00:49:27.480 --> 00:49:29.414
divorce was final by the end of 2024.
离婚将于 2024 年底最终完成。

00:49:29.414 --> 00:49:36.211
As I started to listen to the podcast after its premiere and watch the episodes again, all my nascent romanticism came back to me.
当我在首播后开始听播客并再次观看剧集时，我所有新生的浪漫主义又回到了我的身边。

00:49:36.211 --> 00:49:42.277
By the time your matchmaker episode aired, I had asked Kat out on an official date and we've been dating ever since.
当你的媒人剧集播出时，我已经约凯特出去正式约会，从那时起我们就一直在约会。

00:49:42.277 --> 00:49:48.603
Our friends have commented that it feels like a sitcom ending and I've been quick to point out that it's a hymium ending.
我们的朋友评论说这感觉就像情景喜剧的结局，我很快指出这是一个欢乐的结局。

00:49:48.603 --> 00:49:51.322
You asked what makes this show resonate with people.
你问是什么让这个节目引起人们的共鸣。

00:49:51.322 --> 00:49:55.348
Ted taught me that I could live my life in a different order from my friends.
特德告诉我，我可以按照与朋友们不同的方式生活。

00:49:55.348 --> 00:49:58.904
He taught me that I should take the leap, Metaphorically, of course.
他告诉我，我应该迈出这一步，当然是比喻意义上的。

00:49:58.904 --> 00:50:05.492
He taught me that I didn't need to be the hero of the story for my family and my chosen family to still love me and accept me.
他告诉我，我不需要成为故事的英雄，我的家人和我选择的家人仍然爱我并接受我。

00:50:05.492 --> 00:50:12.760
In a way, I have this show and this podcast to thank for my beautiful family from the bottom of my very full heart from one Ted to another.
在某种程度上，我从心底里感谢这个节目和这个播客，感谢我美丽的家庭，从一个特德到另一个特德。

00:50:12.760 --> 00:50:14.459
All I can say is thank you.
我只能说谢谢。

00:50:14.459 --> 00:50:16.599
Talk about a non-linear narrative.
谈论非线性叙事。

00:50:17.239 --> 00:50:18.119
Really, I know.
真的，我知道。

00:50:18.119 --> 00:50:19.116
That's fantastic.
太棒了。

00:50:19.116 --> 00:50:21.578
That's a beautifully non-linear narrative.
这是一个美妙的非线性叙事。

00:50:21.578 --> 00:50:30.020
I love him deciding in the moment to live his life out of order and out of sequence and have fun with editing in his own life to fix it in post.
我喜欢他此刻决定不按顺序过自己的生活，并享受在自己的生活中进行编辑以在后期修复它的乐趣。

00:50:30.020 --> 00:50:36.117
You know we always talk about like musicians get to soundtrack people's lives like this is a weird show.
你知道，我们总是谈论音乐家为人们的生活配乐，就像这是一场奇怪的演出。

00:50:36.117 --> 00:50:37.934
It's soundtrack people's lives.
它是人们生活的配乐。

00:50:37.934 --> 00:50:40.280
It's like a sitcom that is a soundtrack.
这就像情景喜剧是配乐一样。

00:50:40.280 --> 00:50:41.564
Yeah, that's right.
是的，没错。

00:50:41.564 --> 00:50:43.120
It's a beautiful thing.
这是一件美丽的事情。

00:50:43.120 --> 00:50:43.931
It's a gift.
这是一份礼物。

00:50:43.931 --> 00:50:44.946
Best fans ever.
有史以来最好的粉丝。

00:50:44.946 --> 00:50:46.772
Thanks for sharing stories.
感谢您分享故事。

00:50:46.772 --> 00:50:59.959
If you want to write in a letter or a voice note that maybe we'll play or read on the show, please go to how we made your mother.com hwmym.com and go up to contact and just follow the directions.
